  "answer_text": "## Spiegel Home Catalog Shopping \u2014 What You Need to Know\n\nHere's a comprehensive overview of **Spiegel** and its current status for online/catalog shopping:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcd6 About Spiegel\n\nSpiegel was an **American direct marketing retailer founded in 1865** by Joseph Spiegel. The company published a catalog \u2014 like its competitors Sears, Aldens, and Montgomery Ward \u2014 which advertised various brands of apparel, accessories, and footwear, as well as housewares, toys, tools, and electronics.\n\nSpiegel delivered its first mail-order catalog in **1905**, and by 1925, the retailer had **10 million customers**. Spiegel's buyers, who went to Paris fashion shows, introduced American women to European fashion trends.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Current Status (2026): No Longer Operating\n\nAs of **January 2026**, the short answer is: **you can no longer order from Spiegel.**\n\nSpiegel ran from 1865 to roughly **2019**, when the brand quietly went dark under Patriarch Partners.\n\nAs of this writing, **spiegel.com does not resolve to a working storefront**. There is **no Spiegel print catalog** being mailed in the United States, and no credible news of a brand revival, a buyer, or a relaunch has been found for 2024 or 2025.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udecd\ufe0f Where to Find Vintage Spiegel Catalogs & Items\n\nIf you're a collector or nostalgic shopper, you still have some options:\n\n- **eBay:** Vintage Spiegel clothing turns up regularly on resale sites, and there is a **small collector market for the older catalogs** themselves on eBay.\n\n- **Etsy:** You can find items like **Spiegel 1970 Fall/Winter Fashion Vintage Catalogs** and rare vintage Spiegel catalog items from the 1970s on Etsy.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd04 Alternatives to Spiegel\n\nFor shoppers looking for a similar experience, **Talbots, Soft Surroundings, Appleseed's, and Roaman's** are all still operating and still mailing print catalogs in 2026.\n\nAdditionally, Spiegel had long been known as an American mail-order fixture built around **women's apparel** balancing current trends with accessible pricing, covering dresses, denim, swim, travel pieces, and accessories for the office, weekend, and special occasions. These alternatives carry a similar spirit.\n\n---\n\n**In summary**, Spiegel no longer operates as an active online or print catalog retailer. For vintage items, check **eBay** or **Etsy**, and for new shopping, explore alternatives like **Talbots**, **Roaman's**, or **Soft Surroundings**.",
